# FORENSIC FIX (new-audit Medium finding): wp-cron-run.sh and
# wp-db-backup.sh below each now hold their own mkdir-based lock (matching
# update.sh's existing convention) before doing anything state-changing,
# so a slow run no longer overlaps with the next scheduled tick of itself.
#
# Weekly container image update check (Sunday 04:00 UTC — dry run only)
0 4 * * 0 podman auto-update --dry-run 2>&1 | logger -t podman-autoupdate
# WordPress system cron — replaces unreliable WP-Cron (which only fires on
# page loads). DISABLE_WP_CRON=true is set in WORDPRESS_CONFIG_EXTRA.
# Runs every 5 min; WordPress schedules (backups, updates, email) fire on time.
*/5 * * * * /usr/local/bin/wp-cron-run.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
# Daily MariaDB backup — verified logical dump (v7-13, was pipe-to-gzip).
# Now runs a dedicated script that checks mariadb-dump's own exit status,
# confirms the dump completed to its own marker, verifies the gzip
# archive, and rotates old backups ONLY after all three checks pass.
0 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/wp-db-backup.sh
# FORENSIC FIX (new-audit High finding): auto re-block the uploads-php
# PHP-execution escape hatch if it's been left open too long (see
# wp-hardening.sh's UPLOADS_PHP_MARKER / check-expiry). Silent no-op unless
# it's actually open past the limit, so this doesn't add routine noise.
*/15 * * * * /usr/local/bin/wp-hardening.sh check-expiry >/dev/null 2>&1
# WordPress plugin/theme/core update check (Monday 07:00 UTC). Reports via
# syslog only when something is actually pending, so it doesn't become noise
# the operator learns to ignore. Never auto-updates -- see wp-plugins.sh for
# why that's deliberate rather than an omission.
0 7 * * 1 /usr/local/bin/wp-plugins.sh check >/dev/null 2>&1
# Daily malware and integrity scan (03:30 UTC). Runs the QUICK profile:
# structural checks, core-vs-pinned-image comparison, and database analysis.
# These are the high-signal, low-noise layers. YARA and ClamAV are excluded
# from the daily job deliberately -- YARA because a full-tree signature scan
# is heavy enough to matter on a small VM, ClamAV because of its memory
# footprint. Reports via syslog only when something is found, so a clean day
# is silent and the operator does not learn to ignore it.
30 3 * * * /usr/local/bin/wp-malware-scan.sh quick >/dev/null 2>&1 || logger -t wp-malware "scan reported findings — run: wp-malware-scan.sh status"
# Weekly full scan including YARA (Sunday 03:45 UTC).
45 3 * * 0 /usr/local/bin/wp-malware-scan.sh yara >/dev/null 2>&1 || logger -t wp-malware "weekly YARA scan reported findings — run: wp-malware-scan.sh status"
# Daily vulnerability scan of installed plugins and themes (06:30 UTC).
# Wordfence Intelligence only -- free, no key, and fetched as one bulk feed
# that is queried locally, so the site's plugin inventory is never sent
# anywhere. Silent unless something installed actually matches a disclosed
# vulnerability.
30 6 * * * /usr/local/bin/wp-vuln-cron.sh
